{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25600130",
      "title": "Another Look At State In React Apps",
      "sourceHash": "278dd5f8b0549da64036ddec9a48f103dee5996399b237b74b71d4a768d7fe13",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.15,
          "end": 5.1,
          "en": "So what is Redux?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.1,
          "end": 9.85,
          "en": "Redux is a state management system for a cross-component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 9.85,
          "end": 12.14,
          "en": "or app-wide state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.14,
          "end": 16.81,
          "en": "So it helps us manage state, data that changes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 16.81,
          "end": 18.85,
          "en": "and affects our application",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 18.85,
          "end": 20.88,
          "en": "and what we display on the screen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.88,
          "end": 24.89,
          "en": "It helps us manage such data across multiple components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.89,
          "end": 27.15,
          "en": "or even the complete app.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.15,
          "end": 29.71,
          "en": "Now just to make sure that we're all on the same page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.71,
          "end": 34.24,
          "en": "we did of course use state a lot in this course already",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.24,
          "end": 39.23,
          "en": "with the use state hook or also with use reducer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 39.23,
          "end": 43.49,
          "en": "And indeed those hooks exist to allow us to manage data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 43.49,
          "end": 46.23,
          "en": "that typically changes for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 46.23,
          "end": 50.59,
          "en": "when the user clicks a button and we're changes to that data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 50.59,
          "end": 55.24,
          "en": "then typically lead to the UI being updated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 55.24,
          "end": 59.86,
          "en": "We use React's State Management Hooks like use state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 59.86,
          "end": 63.28,
          "en": "so that we can tell React that some data changed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 63.28,
          "end": 66.67,
          "en": "and so that it then updates the UI for us.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 66.67,
          "end": 69.17,
          "en": "That's what we did through out this course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 69.17,
          "end": 71.33,
          "en": "And that is what state is all about.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 71.33,
          "end": 74.368,
          "en": "But we can split the definition of state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 74.368,
          "end": 78.61,
          "en": "into three main kinds of state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 78.61,
          "end": 82.78,
          "en": "We have a local state and we also have cross-component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 82.78,
          "end": 84.67,
          "en": "and app-wide state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 84.67,
          "end": 87.15,
          "en": "Now these are not hard definitions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 87.15,
          "end": 90.28,
          "en": "these are just definitions which you will see a lot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 90.28,
          "end": 94.44,
          "en": "or these are separations of state which you see a lot",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 94.44,
          "end": 97.05,
          "en": "and therefore I also like to use them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 97.05,
          "end": 99.32,
          "en": "Now what is a local state?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 99.32,
          "end": 104.32,
          "en": "Local state is state so data which changes that affects DUI",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 104.97,
          "end": 107.78999999999999,
          "en": "which belongs to a single component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 107.78999999999999,
          "end": 110.78999999999999,
          "en": "And for example, if we listen to a user input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 110.78999999999999,
          "end": 113.91,
          "en": "and we use useState to store that input",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 113.91,
          "end": 117.50999999999999,
          "en": "with every keystroke in a state variable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 117.50999999999999,
          "end": 122.03,
          "en": "Or we have a button that toggles some detailed field.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 122.03,
          "end": 124.71,
          "en": "So if we click that button we show the details",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 124.71,
          "end": 126.91,
          "en": "if we click it again we hide them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 126.91,
          "end": 129.67,
          "en": "That would be local state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 129.67,
          "end": 132.96,
          "en": "And typically we manage such local state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 132.96,
          "end": 136.34,
          "en": "inside of a component with useState",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 136.34,
          "end": 140.193,
          "en": "or if it's more complex maybe with useReducer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 141.45,
          "end": 144.61,
          "en": "Now we also often have state that affects not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 144.61,
          "end": 148.69,
          "en": "just one component but multiple components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 148.69,
          "end": 150.98,
          "en": "That would be cross component state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 150.98,
          "end": 153.7,
          "en": "For example, if we have a button that opens",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 153.7,
          "end": 158.43,
          "en": "or closes a modal overlay such a modal component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 158.43,
          "end": 161.1,
          "en": "might affect multiple components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 161.1,
          "end": 165.64,
          "en": "and the trigger for opening the modal is per definition",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 165.64,
          "end": 167.31,
          "en": "not inside of the modal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 167.31,
          "end": 169.92000000000002,
          "en": "On the apprehend the modal might be closed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 169.92000000000002,
          "end": 173.49,
          "en": "by clicking a button which is inside of that modal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 173.49,
          "end": 176.5,
          "en": "So then we have multiple components working together",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 176.5,
          "end": 179.48,
          "en": "to display and hide a modal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 179.48,
          "end": 182.97,
          "en": "And we can also implement that with useState",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 182.97,
          "end": 187.13,
          "en": "or useReducer we then just need to pass props around",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 187.13,
          "end": 189.87,
          "en": "so we need to build those prop chains",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 189.87,
          "end": 193.82,
          "en": "or do this prop drilling as it's also called",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 193.82,
          "end": 197.41,
          "en": "where we pass drops across multiple components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 197.41,
          "end": 200.728,
          "en": "where we also might pass functions as props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 200.728,
          "end": 202.73,
          "en": "across multiple components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 202.73,
          "end": 205.85,
          "en": "so that these different components can work together",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 205.85,
          "end": 208.21,
          "en": "and manage state together.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 208.21,
          "end": 210.12,
          "en": "And that's not bad or anything like that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 210.12,
          "end": 213.8,
          "en": "it's just a little bit more complex than local state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 213.8,
          "end": 216.16,
          "en": "And sometimes we also have State",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 216.16,
          "end": 219.62,
          "en": "that does not just affect multiple components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 219.62,
          "end": 223.67000000000002,
          "en": "but basically all components of an application.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 223.67000000000002,
          "end": 228.37,
          "en": "Now when that happens we could call this app-wide state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 228.37,
          "end": 232.48,
          "en": "and an example here would be user authentication.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 232.48,
          "end": 236.4,
          "en": "If I log in we might need to change the navigation bar",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 236.4,
          "end": 239.32,
          "en": "because we now show new options",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 239.32,
          "end": 242.47,
          "en": "and we also certainly affect a lot of other components",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 242.47,
          "end": 244.923,
          "en": "which now show more or less data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 245.83,
          "end": 248.84,
          "en": "So that would be an example for app-wide state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 248.84,
          "end": 252.67,
          "en": "And we can also manage this with the useState, useReducer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 252.67,
          "end": 254.95,
          "en": "and then by passing state values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 254.95,
          "end": 258.31,
          "en": "and updating functions around full props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 258.31,
          "end": 260.47,
          "en": "That's what we did through out this course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 260.47,
          "end": 263.01,
          "en": "and the data of course works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 263.01,
          "end": 266.06,
          "en": "Now for cross-component and app-wide state",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 266.06,
          "end": 269.79,
          "en": "passing around data and updating function fruit props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 269.79,
          "end": 272.13,
          "en": "can become cumbersome though.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 272.13,
          "end": 275.06,
          "en": "And that's why we did learn about React Context",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 275.06,
          "end": 276.44,
          "en": "before in the course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 276.44,
          "end": 280.14,
          "en": "React Context is a built in feature in React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 280.14,
          "end": 282.55,
          "en": "that makes managing cross-component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 282.55,
          "end": 284.93,
          "en": "or application wide state easier.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 284.93,
          "end": 287.82,
          "en": "So that's one way of simplifying cross-component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 287.82,
          "end": 290.21,
          "en": "and app-wide state management.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 290.21,
          "end": 292.94,
          "en": "Redux solves the same problem.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 292.94,
          "end": 297.94,
          "en": "So both React Context and Redux are there to help us manage",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 298.17,
          "end": 301.39,
          "en": "such cross-component or app-wide States.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 301.39,
          "end": 304.61,
          "en": "And that of course brings up an important question.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 304.61,
          "end": 309.21,
          "en": "Why do we need Redux if we already have React Context",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 309.21,
          "end": 312.493,
          "en": "for managing state that affects multiple components?",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}